  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Francis Al\u00ffs. The Nature of the Game (2023), published by Leuven University Press, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 1,489 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Francis Al\u00ffs. The Nature of the Game by Gerard-Jan Claes and St\u00e9phane Symons was published by Leuven University Press in 2023. Conceptually, the work connects to Seriousness, Presentation (obstetrics), Face (sociological concept), Cartography and History.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,489 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>",
